{#
   Your Role (#role). Reworked to the redesign's two-column layout: the "YOU
   CONTROL" list on the left, the Personal Assistant card on the right.

   Note the id changed from #your-role to #role to match the design's anchor
   (the header nav links to it). Nothing else in the repo linked to #your-role —
   it was referenced only by _nav.html.twig, which this pass rewrote.

   The screenshot that used to close this section is gone, along with the rest of
   the page's screenshots; there is no sprite scene in its place because the
   design does not put one here.

   The "YOUR STAFF HANDLE" block below the two columns is NOT in the design.
   It is kept because it is the only place on the page that says what each of the
   five staff roles actually decides, which is the substance behind the
   delegation pillar — losing it would thin out the pitch rather than simplify
   it. It is placed after the designed columns, as a full-width block, so the
   layout the design specifies renders exactly as drawn above it.
#}
<section class="role-section" id="role" aria-labelledby="role-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="role-split">
            <div class="role-main">
                <div class="section-label">Your Role</div>
                <h2 class="section-title" id="role-title">YOU'RE THE OWNER. NOT THE GAFFER.</h2>
                <p class="section-sub">Step into the boardroom and build a football powerhouse from the ground up. Start at the bottom of an {{ world.totals.tierCount }}-tier national ladder, create your owner, and take charge of a modest setup: a basic squad, a handful of introductory coaches and foundational backroom staff. Direct the club's money, and play the long game.</p>

                <h3 class="role-list-title pixel">YOU CONTROL</h3>
                <ul class="role-control-list">
                    <li>Capital allocation and financial decisions</li>
                    <li>Facility investment and infrastructure build-out</li>
                    <li>Staff hiring across six roles</li>
                    <li>Sponsor negotiations and investor equity deals</li>
                    <li>Agent and guardian relations</li>
                    <li>Club identity</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <aside class="role-pa" aria-labelledby="role-pa-title">
                <div class="role-pa-title pixel" id="role-pa-title">YOUR PERSONAL ASSISTANT</div>
                <p class="role-pa-intro">Not a hire: your own briefing, pulled live from the same data your staff work from.</p>

                <div class="role-pa-row">
                    <div class="role-pa-head vt is-mint">Dressing room harmony</div>
                    <p>The pulse of team chemistry and morale, before it becomes a problem.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="role-pa-row">
                    <div class="role-pa-head vt is-cyan">Tactical and physical health</div>
                    <p>Is the XI your Manager wants actually fit to play?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="role-pa-row">
                    <div class="role-pa-head vt is-gold">Supporter pulse</div>
                    <p>Fan sentiment, attendance and outlook. The crowd notices every call you make.</p>
                </div>
            </aside>
        </div>

        <div class="role-staff">
            <h3 class="role-list-title pixel">YOUR STAFF HANDLE</h3>
            <ul class="role-staff-list">
                <li><span class="role-staff-name">Chairman</span>Agrees the season mandate with your Manager — his job security hinges on hitting it. Signs off Facility Manager discounts and investor offers, balances the operating reserve, and plans excursions to keep the squad onside.</li>
                <li><span class="role-staff-name">Director of Football</span>Recruitment priorities, scouting reach, and the free-agent panic button when a position can't field an XI. Manages coach and scout contracts, including individual coach-to-player assignments.</li>
                <li><span class="role-staff-name">Manager</span>Formation, playing style and matchday selection. Resolves squad conflicts and player requests — override him anytime, at a morale cost.</li>
                <li><span class="role-staff-name">Facility Manager</span>Proactive or reactive maintenance — stop campus decay before it hits performance and player morale.</li>
                <li><span class="role-staff-name">Scout</span>Talent identification, evaluation ability and player reports.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="role-footer">Delegate everything to your DoF and Manager and focus on the boardroom — or override every decision yourself. The level of involvement is always your choice. One warning: staff whose morale collapses will resign, and a backroom departure damages squad-wide morale and erases relationships that took seasons to build.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
